  "vibe": "Sun-bleached concrete (#d8d4cc) under charcoal ink and one traffic-cone orange (#ff4d00), with Bungee stacking headlines like a hand-painted park sign. A single ink line draws the coping of a bowl right across the frame, and an orange board actually skates it — rolling wall to wall, popping about 200px into the air at each lip and whipping a full 160° rotation before it lands, wobbling 8° through the flat. An orange grind-spark scrawl sits in the top corner; pebbles scatter on the deck. Everything slams: titles and items share the hardest entrance, the camera spins and skews 6°, montage tiles cock up to 4°. Statements go black, the closer floods orange. Mechanics: a combo-line key cursor, a rebuild progress bar, park alerts and a rolling morph. Best for skate shops, DIY builds and scrappy local sport.",
